questions.explanation:
Fragile X is the second most common genetic cause for intellectual impairment, occurring in 1/4000 males and 1/8000 females. Down‘s
syndrome tos the list and occurs in 1/1000 children. Prader Willi occurs in 1/10-30,000 people; Angelman syndrome occurs in 1/12-20,000;
William‘s syndrome occurs in 1/7500-12000 people.
